  {
    "episode_id": 90754,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90754.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 91,
    "turn_text": "Bob Roll, who you know is the announcer who covers the tour de France, the guy who's got the gap tooth. And he was announcing for this race. He said, you know, watching a crit is a lot of fun because they keep going by and because it was all these women's teams going. It was just really cool, because they had been watching the Tour de France for a couple of years and saying, why is there no women's Tour de France? It's a really good question, like they should be. And then we went up. And things you think about when you've got daughters, it was just nice to go and share with them and see this guy who they had seen on the television carrying the Tour de France who was now out there announcing you know, for the, these just, you know, unbelievably talented sprinters, you know, essentially.",
